AB  - A pathogenic strain, adaptive to the ecosystem on North China, of Beauveria bassiana was isolated and selected from muscardine Dendrolimus tabulaeformis. Sporulation, conidial germination rate and hyphal growth were determined. Results showed that germination rate was highest (91.6%) at 25C. When pine caterpillars in 3 -4 instars were inoculated with spore suspension at five concentrations (1.0 10~(6), 5.0 10~(6), 1.0 10~(7), 5.0 10~(7), 1.0 10~(8)n/ml)under 25 1C and the RH 75% 5% in lab, mortality ranged 67.49% -95.13 % at the 10th day of inoculation. Under natural conditions with low temperature and RH, the correction mortality of D. tabulaeformis at the 23th day of infection could reach 50.0% - 78.4% . When wettable powder (4.5 10~(9) spores/g) of B. bassiana was applied in November and next March around rootstock, mortality of larvae of D. tabulaeforrnis was 50% -78%.
